IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g7-interpretation`
IMPORT `g7-vintages`
IMPORT `g7-commencement`

-- int-commencement.l4: integration point IP4. Each headline function of the integration layer rests on named Articles and Schedules of the Law; it answers only if every one of them was in force
-- on the day asked, and otherwise REFUSES with a reason that names the unit and the day it came into force. Groups G2 to G9 do not gate themselves (PLAN section 10, item 2).
-- GENERATED by work/integrator/gen_commencement.py. The stage of each Article was READ from G7's `Commencement: the stage in which the unit was brought into force` (favoured reading) when
-- this file was written, and the tests (int-tests-commencement.l4) assert, for every Article and Schedule, that the refusal below occurs on exactly the days G7 says the unit is not in force.
-- The Law's Parts and their stages: Parts 1 to 3, Article 32, Articles 38 to 43 and the Schedules from 21 November 2014; Parts 4, 5, 7, Articles 33 to 37 from 1 May 2018; Part 6 from 1 January 2019 (R&O.17/2018).
-- A REFUSE message is a string literal, so there is one literal per unit; they are polymorphic (a refusal at any type).

§ `Integration layer -- commencement (IP4)`

-- The answer of the gate, as a value, for a caller that wants to handle 'not in force' without a refusal.
DECLARE `Gate on a day` IS ONE OF
    `every unit the question rests on is in force`
    `a unit the question rests on is not in force` HAS unit IS A `Unit of the Law` @desc The first unit, in the order the question lists them, that was not in force

-- The first of the units that is not in force on the day, or NOTHING when all are.
GIVEN units IS A LIST OF `Unit of the Law` @desc The units (Articles as now numbered, Schedules) the question rests on, in order
      day IS A DATE @desc The day on which the question is asked
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The readings of group G7 (the numbering the commencement table speaks in, and the treatment of a Part in two stages)
GIVETH A `Gate on a day`
`Int the gate on the day for` units day interp MEANS
    CONSIDER (filter (GIVEN u YIELD NOT (`Commencement: the unit of the Law is in force on` u day interp)) units)
      WHEN EMPTY THEN `every unit the question rests on is in force`
      WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN `a unit the question rests on is not in force` first

-- The named refusal for one Article as now numbered or one Schedule.
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
      unit IS A `Unit of the Law` @desc The unit that was not in force
GIVETH AN a
`Int refusal: a unit of the Law was not in force on the day asked` unit MEANS
    CONSIDER unit
      WHEN `an Article of the Law as now numbered` article THEN `Int refusal: an Article was not in force on the day asked` article
      WHEN `a Schedule to the Law` schedule THEN `Int refusal: a Schedule was not in force on the day asked` schedule
      WHEN `a Part of the Law` part THEN REFUSE "a Part of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 on which this question rests was not in force on the day asked"
      WHEN `an Article of the Law as originally numbered` original THEN REFUSE "an Article, as originally numbered, of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 on which this question rests was not in force on the day asked"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
      article IS A NUMBER @desc The Article as now numbered
GIVETH AN a
`Int refusal: an Article was not in force on the day asked` article MEANS
    BRANCH
      IF article EQUALS 1 THEN REFUSE "Article 1 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 1) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 21 November 2014"
      IF article EQUALS 2 THEN REFUSE "Article 2 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 1) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 21 November 2014"
      IF article EQUALS 3 THEN REFUSE "Article 3 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 2) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 21 November 2014"
      IF article EQUALS 4 THEN REFUSE "Article 4 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 2) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 21 November 2014"
      IF article EQUALS 5 THEN REFUSE "Article 5 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 3) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 21 November 2014"
      IF article EQUALS 6 THEN REFUSE "Article 6 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 3) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 21 November 2014"
      IF article EQUALS 7 THEN REFUSE "Article 7 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 3) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 21 November 2014"
      IF article EQUALS 8 THEN REFUSE "Article 8 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 4) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
      IF article EQUALS 9 THEN REFUSE "Article 9 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 4) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
      IF article EQUALS 10 THEN REFUSE "Article 10 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 4) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
      IF article EQUALS 11 THEN REFUSE "Article 11 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 4) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
      IF article EQUALS 12 THEN REFUSE "Article 12 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 4) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
      IF article EQUALS 13 THEN REFUSE "Article 13 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 4) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
      IF article EQUALS 14 THEN REFUSE "Article 14 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 4) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
      IF article EQUALS 15 THEN REFUSE "Article 15 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 4) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
      IF article EQUALS 16 THEN REFUSE "Article 16 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 4) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
      IF article EQUALS 17 THEN REFUSE "Article 17 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 4) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
      IF article EQUALS 18 THEN REFUSE "Article 18 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 5) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
      IF article EQUALS 19 THEN REFUSE "Article 19 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 5) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
      IF article EQUALS 20 THEN REFUSE "Article 20 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 5) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
      IF article EQUALS 21 THEN REFUSE "Article 21 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 6) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 January 2019"
      IF article EQUALS 22 THEN REFUSE "Article 22 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 6) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 January 2019"
      IF article EQUALS 23 THEN REFUSE "Article 23 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 6) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 January 2019"
      IF article EQUALS 24 THEN REFUSE "Article 24 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 6) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 January 2019"
      IF article EQUALS 25 THEN REFUSE "Article 25 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 6) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 January 2019"
      IF article EQUALS 26 THEN REFUSE "Article 26 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 7) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
      IF article EQUALS 27 THEN REFUSE "Article 27 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 7) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
      IF article EQUALS 28 THEN REFUSE "Article 28 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 7) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
      IF article EQUALS 29 THEN REFUSE "Article 29 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 7) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
      IF article EQUALS 30 THEN REFUSE "Article 30 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 7) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
      IF article EQUALS 31 THEN REFUSE "Article 31 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 7) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
      IF article EQUALS 32 THEN REFUSE "Article 32 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 8) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 21 November 2014"
      IF article EQUALS 33 THEN REFUSE "Article 33 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 8) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
      IF article EQUALS 34 THEN REFUSE "Article 34 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 8) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
      IF article EQUALS 35 THEN REFUSE "Article 35 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 8) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
      IF article EQUALS 36 THEN REFUSE "Article 36 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 8) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
      IF article EQUALS 37 THEN REFUSE "Article 37 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 9) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
      IF article EQUALS 38 THEN REFUSE "Article 38 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 9) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 21 November 2014"
      IF article EQUALS 39 THEN REFUSE "Article 39 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 9) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 21 November 2014"
      IF article EQUALS 40 THEN REFUSE "Article 40 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 9) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 21 November 2014"
      IF article EQUALS 41 THEN REFUSE "Article 41 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 9) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 21 November 2014"
      IF article EQUALS 42 THEN REFUSE "Article 42 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 9) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 21 November 2014"
      IF article EQUALS 43 THEN REFUSE "Article 43 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 9) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 21 November 2014"
      OTHERWISE REFUSE "the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 has no such Article as now numbered (Articles 1 to 43)"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
      schedule IS A NUMBER @desc The Schedule, 1 or 2
GIVETH AN a
`Int refusal: a Schedule was not in force on the day asked` schedule MEANS
    BRANCH
      IF schedule EQUALS 1 THEN REFUSE "Schedule 1 to the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 21 November 2014"
      IF schedule EQUALS 2 THEN REFUSE "Schedule 2 to the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 21 November 2014"
      OTHERWISE REFUSE "the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 has no such Schedule (Schedules 1 and 2)"

-- The headline wrapper: the answer if every unit is in force, the named refusal otherwise. `answer` is evaluated only when the gate lets it through.
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
      units IS A LIST OF `Unit of the Law` @desc The units the question rests on
      day IS A DATE @desc The day on which the question is asked
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` @desc The readings of group G7
      answer IS AN a @desc The answer, evaluated only if every unit is in force
GIVETH AN a
`Int the answer if every unit is in force` units day interp answer MEANS
    CONSIDER (`Int the gate on the day for` units day interp)
      WHEN `every unit the question rests on is in force` THEN answer
      WHEN `a unit the question rests on is not in force` unit THEN `Int refusal: a unit of the Law was not in force on the day asked` unit

-- Short spellings of the units, so that a headline lists them as the Law does.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Unit of the Law`
`Int Article` n MEANS `an Article of the Law as now numbered` n

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Unit of the Law`
`Int Schedule` n MEANS `a Schedule to the Law` n

